<newsitem itemid="719258" id="root" date="1997-07-10" xml:lang="en">
<title>CHINA: Sing Tao year net returns to profit.</title>
<headline>Sing Tao year net returns to profit.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	  6.3 gain     vs 34.4 loss</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)   4.0	    vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	 nil	    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			   26.93 profit vs 146.42 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		    1,938.89     vs 1,609.71 (see note)</p>
<p>    Company name		Sing Tao Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		 August 14-22</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	  August 28</p>
<p>NOTE - Sing Tao is a newspaper publisher and printer.</p>
<p>The corresponding turnover has been restated to conform to the current year's presentation.</p>
<p>Total dividend for the year is four H.K. cents vs two cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
